  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197356",
      "title": "Styling React Native Apps",
      "lectureOrder": 15,
      "videoOrder": 13,
      "sourceHash": "552f0fb8a55b45c13a9db4f140dc5743f3256b1144d6d9cf554bbc2a9e366ba2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 5.18,
          "en": "So let's dive into styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.18,
          "end": 6.88,
          "en": "And here you learned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.88,
          "end": 10.43,
          "en": "that there is no CSS support in the React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.43,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "so we don't add CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 15.46,
          "en": "or use the CSS language in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.46,
          "end": 19.64,
          "en": "but you learned that we have two main ways of adding styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.64,
          "end": 21.47,
          "en": "by either adding styles in line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.47,
          "end": 24.65,
          "en": "by passing a style object to props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.65,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "or by defining a separate object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 29.173,
          "en": "which is then also passed through props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.59,
          "end": 33.83,
          "en": "Now we do define our styles in JavaScript then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.83,
          "end": 36.95,
          "en": "but the JavaScript properties we can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.95,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "are inspired by the CSS language",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "though it's only a subset of the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 45.95,
          "en": "and features supported by CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.95,
          "end": 50.093,
          "en": "and not all the names are exactly the same, as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.16,
          "end": 53.89,
          "en": "But let's now see how styles can be applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.89,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "For that, we can use the style prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 60.23,
          "en": "which is not supported on all elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.23,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "but on some elements, for example on the view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 64.593,
          "en": "but also on the text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.47,
          "end": 68.41,
          "en": "For example, here on let's say this text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.41,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "we can add the style prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 74.103,
          "en": "And then as a value, you can pass a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.12,
          "end": 76.81,
          "en": "And in this object you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.81,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "all the supported style properties and React Native decides",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "which properties are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 88.1,
          "en": "And these are the properties that are similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.1,
          "end": 91.85300000000001,
          "en": "to the CSS properties, but not exactly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.92,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "For example, here on this text, we could add a margin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 98.99000000000001,
          "en": "And as you see, as I start typing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.65299999999999,
          "en": "we get this nice auto completion here in VS Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 106.55,
          "en": "We get this automatically because VS Code understands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.55,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "which kind of properties can be set on this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 112.503,
          "en": "that is passed to the style prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.44200000000001,
          "end": 116.22999999999999,
          "en": "Now, here we could add a margin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.22999999999999,
          "end": 119.93,
          "en": "either in one specific direction or in multiple directions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.93,
          "end": 121.696,
          "en": "by combining multiple properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.696,
          "end": 124.82300000000001,
          "en": "or in all directions by setting margin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.07,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "Now different style properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 131.24,
          "en": "need different kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.24,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "And you will see many examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 137,
          "en": "and learn which kind of value goes into which style property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137,
          "end": 138.92000000000002,
          "en": "throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.92000000000002,
          "end": 142.63,
          "en": "Margin, for example, typically wants a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.63,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "and this number will then be translated to pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 147.88,
          "en": "which are automatically adjusted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.88,
          "end": 150.163,
          "en": "to the device pixel density.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.3,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "For example, here we could enter 16",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 156.77,
          "en": "to have a margin of 16 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.77,
          "end": 159.7,
          "en": "If we save this, we got some spacing around this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.7,
          "end": 161.57,
          "en": "Now it's not super good to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.57,
          "end": 165.623,
          "en": "because we don't know exactly where the text box ends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.51,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "To make this a bit more visible, we could add a border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 174.02,
          "en": "Now in Vanilla CSS, you could add a border,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.02,
          "end": 175.94299999999998,
          "en": "like this for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.15,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "This would add a red border with one pixel width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 184.5,
          "en": "around an element in Vanilla CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.5,
          "end": 185.98,
          "en": "But if I type this kind of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.98,
          "end": 188.95,
          "en": "and saved this here in React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.95,
          "end": 191.6,
          "en": "we actually got no effect here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.6,
          "end": 194.3,
          "en": "and I got a error here in the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.3,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "and a warning here on my simulator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "We can click on this to get more details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 205.803,
          "en": "and we see that this is an invalid value for border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.92000000000002,
          "end": 210.11,
          "en": "Actually the key border already is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.11,
          "end": 211.34,
          "en": "So it's not even the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.34,
          "end": 213.653,
          "en": "but border is not a supported key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.37,
          "end": 217.71,
          "en": "The reason for this is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 220.34,
          "en": "that this border property doesn't exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.34,
          "end": 224.92000000000002,
          "en": "I mentioned that the styling language is inspired by CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.92000000000002,
          "end": 227.913,
          "en": "and close to CSS, but it's not exactly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 231.22,
          "en": "Instead, as we type border,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.22,
          "end": 234.653,
          "en": "we see that various properties exist, which we can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.69,
          "end": 238.57,
          "en": "For example, we can set a border with property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.57,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "and this again wants a number to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 245.143,
          "en": "a certain border width in pixels, like one, one pixel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.29,
          "end": 248.51,
          "en": "or two or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.51,
          "end": 251.54,
          "en": "And then we can also set a bordered color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.54,
          "end": 254.74,
          "en": "Now this does not want a number, but instead of string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 254.74,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "and in this string, you could define a hex code value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 263.28,
          "end": 266.09,
          "en": "Or you provide one of the supported shortcuts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.09,
          "end": 270.77,
          "en": "like red or blue or green or black and white.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.77,
          "end": 272.403,
          "en": "And here I will go for red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 276.36,
          "en": "And this will now add a two pixel, white, red border",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 277.743,
          "en": "around this text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.59000000000003,
          "end": 280.7,
          "en": "Now I'll press the auto format shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.7,
          "end": 283.823,
          "en": "to make this a bit easier to read and then save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 287.853,
          "en": "And with this, we now got a border around this text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.87,
          "end": 291.9,
          "en": "The border is pretty close to the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 294.78,
          "en": "but thankfully we can also add some padding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.78,
          "end": 296.96,
          "en": "padding just as in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.96,
          "end": 299.653,
          "en": "is the spacing inside of an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.79,
          "end": 304.62,
          "en": "So here we could add a padding of let's say 16 again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.62,
          "end": 307.96,
          "en": "16 pixels, just as for the margin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.96,
          "end": 312.04,
          "en": "And if we save this and auto format again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.04,
          "end": 316.67,
          "en": "to improve readability, now we got some internal spacing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 316.67,
          "end": 319.64,
          "en": "Now definitely feel free to play around more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.64,
          "end": 322.61,
          "en": "with those style properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.61,
          "end": 325.14,
          "en": "And of course also take a look at the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.14,
          "end": 327.21,
          "en": "to learn more about styling if you want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.21,
          "end": 329.5,
          "en": "but you will see plenty of styling examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 329.5,
          "end": 330.6,
          "en": "throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.6,
          "end": 335.54200000000003,
          "en": "These style properties were all about styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.54200000000003,
          "end": 339.92,
          "en": "the element itself that holds a certain piece of content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 339.92,
          "end": 343.03,
          "en": "We will later also learn about style properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.03,
          "end": 347.32,
          "en": "that help us with laying out multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.32,
          "end": 351.24,
          "en": "and with achieving a certain overall look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 351.24,
          "end": 354.65,
          "en": "But again, that is something we will explore later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 354.65,
          "end": 355.483,
          "en": "For the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 355.483,
          "end": 358.57,
          "en": "I wanna leave this in-line styling approach though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.57,
          "end": 362.13,
          "en": "This approach of defining the styles in the same line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.13,
          "end": 364.263,
          "en": "as we define this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.35,
          "end": 368.92,
          "en": "Because whilst this is possible and allowed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.92,
          "end": 372.423,
          "en": "it's rarely the best way of adding styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 373.34,
          "end": 376.41,
          "en": "So typically we should go for a style sheet objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 376.41,
          "end": 377.38,
          "en": "The reason for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 377.38,
          "end": 380.11,
          "en": "is that this allows us to clearly separate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.11,
          "end": 383.14,
          "en": "our JSX code and our styling code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 383.14,
          "end": 386.24,
          "en": "and it also makes our styles reusable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 386.24,
          "end": 388.28,
          "en": "If we define styles in line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 388.28,
          "end": 390.67,
          "en": "and I want the same styling on this text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 390.67,
          "end": 393.53,
          "en": "I have to copy and paste this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.53,
          "end": 396.09000000000003,
          "en": "so that I can add my style prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 396.09000000000003,
          "end": 398.15,
          "en": "and add the same styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.15,
          "end": 400.7,
          "en": "and I'll auto format this to make it more readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.95,
          "end": 405.74,
          "en": "So now I had to copy and paste to replicate this style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 405.74,
          "end": 408.99,
          "en": "And that is typically something you wanna avoid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 408.99,
          "end": 410.22,
          "en": "What you should instead do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 410.22,
          "end": 413.32,
          "en": "is create a new style sheet object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 413.32,
          "end": 416.43,
          "en": "Or if you already have one, as we have it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 416.43,
          "end": 419.613,
          "en": "you go to this object and you add a new property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.71,
          "end": 422.89,
          "en": "We already have the container property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 422.89,
          "end": 426.14,
          "en": "now on the same level, I'm adding another property.",
